Description: Rekordbox USB tracks with accented filenames load again, and a
 missing file says so instead of ignoring the tap.
 .
 Two halves of one field report: "some tracks do not load". The file in
 question ("BASTI - La Mamá ...") decodes cleanly; what fails is finding it.
 The mount side of the fix lives in pi/usb-mount.sh (FAT sticks are now
 mounted with utf8=1, so the kernel hands back the same UTF-8 bytes rekordbox
 wrote into the PDB). This patch covers what Mixxx itself can do:
 .
 1. When a rekordbox device is imported, a track path containing non-ASCII
    characters that does not exist as written is retried in the other Unicode
    normalisation form (NFC <-> NFD). rekordbox on macOS writes decomposed
    names to FAT32 while the PDB string may be composed, or vice versa, and a
    byte-exact lookup then misses a file that is plainly on the stick. ASCII
    paths never touch the disk, so the import cost is unchanged for them.
 .
 Trimmed for the GRV6 build: the [Library],load_missing banner half was dropped (it only serves the Pioneered skin).
